++
++[lints.rust]
++unexpected_cfgs = { level = "warn", check-cfg = ['cfg(target_os, values("qnx"))'] }
+diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
+index 55eed9e..807561b 100644
+--- a/README.md
++++ b/README.md
+@@ -23,2 +23,8 @@ A list of supported/tested targets can be found in [Actions](https://github.com/
+
++On QNX, `Advice::{Normal, Random, Sequential, WillNeed}` use `posix_madvise`
++access-pattern hints. Valid empty hint ranges succeed without a syscall.
++`UncheckedAdvice::DontNeed` returns `std::io::ErrorKind::Unsupported`: QNX's
++`POSIX_MADV_DONTNEED` does not provide the destructive discard semantics of
++that operation.
++
+ ## License
